<p>Cookies are small files a website stores in your browser. This page explains which ones this site uses and the choices you have.</p>

<h2>What we use</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Type</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>PHPSESSID</code></td><td>Keeps your session and the security token that protects the contact form against cross-site request forgery.</td><td>Strictly necessary, first-party</td><td>Session</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>nx_cookie_notice</code> (local storage)</td><td>Remembers that you have seen and answered the cookie notice, so we do not ask again.</td><td>Strictly necessary, first-party</td><td>12 months</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Strictly necessary items work without consent because the site cannot operate securely without them. We do <b>not</b> currently use analytics, advertising or social-media tracking cookies. If we add any, we will list them here and ask for your consent first.</p>

<h2>Third-party content</h2>
<p>Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts. Google may receive your IP address and browser details when it serves them. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings; the site will still load, but the contact form may stop working. You can change your cookie notice answer at any time:</p>
<p><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline" data-cookie-reset>Reopen cookie notice</button></p>
